# R10: Phillip and Adela Druskenvald in the Lounge Car (G3). Speakers phillip_druskenvald, adela_druskenvald. Region ghostlight_express.
# Started by: the pair at the bar (`meet`, `approach: 3`, `when: not flag.gl_crashed`; later visits start at `return_router`).
# Their regard is two ints, phillip_regard and adela_regard (the book's "first impressions"), read by R12, R16, R22 to R24. Prying, rudeness and
# lies make Phillip button up (`attitude ... indifferent`); nothing here locks anything. The reading is offered from `ask_cards` (adela_reading).
# Drafted by Gemini (Gemini/sent_09_druskenvalds_lounge.txt, reply_09_druskenvalds_lounge.json), edited; see README.md.

~ meet
if flag.gl_lounge_met
-> return_router
endif
set gl_lounge_met
Narrator: A tall, thin gentleman in a striped suit leans against the bar with a silver goat-skull cane, while beside him a lady in a shimmering dress laughs over a champagne flute.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Well now, look what the mist brought in, darling: actual breathing company. Step right up to the bar, my good friends, and name your poison.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, how utterly swell! You have no idea how dull a lounge gets when nobody's heart is beating.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: I'm Adela, and this tall drink of water is my husband, Phillip.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Do say you've come to gossip with us until the wheels stop turning.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Pace yourself, darling, or you'll talk the poor travelers out of their coats before their glasses are full.
interject name:rook_coldwake: High-grade tailoring, zero practical armor. Mind the floor around them.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Silk and silver. Fine blossoms on a strange branch, if the roots hold.
interject name:silas_vane: Folks flashing that much silver at the table usually own the casino.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Oh, look at the sparkle on her! Proper velvet-curtain royalty, darling.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Easy now. Polished manners, sharp scent: they rule this stretch of woods.
interject name:cordelia_skein: What wonderfully lively pulses they imitate. Do ask if we may observe them.
-> menu

~ menu
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Now then, old sports, what'll it be?
* Who are the two of you? -> ask_who
* Where are you headed on this train? -> ask_home
* What business brought you out here? -> ask_business
* Do you ride with the Vagrant often? -> ask_train
* [if flag.gl_phantom_done] We fought a shadowy stowaway in the cars. -> ask_shade
* [if not flag.gl_drinks_had] We wouldn't say no to a drink. -> drinks
* [if not flag.tarot_full_reading] You mentioned reading tarot cards? -> ask_cards
* [if not flag.gl_complimented] You two are the finest sight on this train. -> compliment
* [if not flag.gl_pried] How does a lord end up ruling a ghost realm? -> pry
* [if flag.haint_songstress_met and not flag.haint_songstress_done and not flag.haint_songstress_destroyed] Who is the pale woman humming by the window? -> ask_singer
* [if not flag.gl_painting_asked] That coastal painting on the wall just moved. -> ask_painting
* We'll leave you to your drinks for now. -> leave

~ ask_who
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Phillip Druskenvald, at your service, and this is my wife, Adela. Folks around here call us lord and lady of the realm, though we don't stand on grand titles.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: A title is just a heavy hat that ruins a good haircut, wouldn't you say?
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: I only ask that life, and the life after it, be a grand old time for everyone at the table.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Listen to Philly playing modest, when he loves a grand entrance more than anyone alive!
-> menu

~ ask_home
adela_druskenvald [smile]: We're bound for home, darling: Chateau Clair de Lune, every arch and staircase built to my own design.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: It has twelve fireplaces and a ballroom with a ceiling like the inside of a seashell.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: You simply must come to dinner once we're settled, I won't take no for an answer.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Consider the invitation engraved in silver, friends: our table is always better with fresh stories.
-> menu

~ ask_business
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: Oh, provincial affairs out along the border, dull as dishwater. Nothing but ledgers, signatures, and men clearing their throats in drafty halls.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: The sort of travel that makes a man deeply grateful for a well-stocked bar car.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: The paperwork was a frightful bore, darling, though meeting all the strange little townsfolk was the bee's knees.
-> menu

~ ask_train
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: We've ridden the Ghostlight Express for ages, and I wouldn't trade it for a golden carriage. Our Vagrant is the finest conductor on any line.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Keeps the rails smooth, the ice cold, and the riffraff out of the upholstery.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: And have you heard him play that fiddle of his? He's an absolute peach, spikes in his hat and all.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Whenever we travel, we wouldn't dream of booking with anyone else.
-> menu

~ ask_shade
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: A shadowy stowaway causing a ruckus in the cars? I wouldn't lose a wink of sleep over it, old sport.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: The Vagrant knows every bolt and rivet on this train, and he'll sort out any gatecrasher before the ice melts.
adela_druskenvald [sad]: Still, a cold shadow slipping between the carriages gives a girl a queer little shiver down her spine.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Good thing we have four strapping heroes aboard to keep the bogeymen polite!
-> menu

~ drinks
set gl_drinks_had
set phillip_regard += 1
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Have whatever you like, my friends, the bar is hardly short and the tab is mine.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: A dry martini, a neat rye, or something warm from an orchard you remember: just say the word.
Narrator: You barely speak a name before the glasses sit beside your elbows, chilled or steaming just right. Each cup holds the exact drop your tongue was secretly asking for.
-> menu

~ ask_cards
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, I thought you'd never ask, I've been itching to shuffle my deck since we boarded!
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Step close and let's see what the pasteboards have to say about your road ahead, darling.
-> ghostlight_express/adela_reading:offer

~ compliment
set gl_complimented
set phillip_regard += 1
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Well now, you have a remarkably discerning eye for quality, my friend. A man tries to keep up standards, even out in the fog.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Darling, did you hear that? Plainly we are traveling with people of rare breeding and exquisite taste.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Put your feathers down, Philly, they're laying it on with a silver trowel and you're eating up every spoonful.
-> menu

# Prying: Phillip closes the subject like a door. The Insight read is spent if it fails, and the apology is always there.
~ pry
set gl_pried
set phillip_regard -= 1
attitude phillip_druskenvald indifferent
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: My dear fellow, what a barrage of ledger-keeper's questions for a pleasant evening in the lounge. Whose land, which charter, where the road began: you sound like those clerks we just left behind.
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: A gentleman does not dig up the cellar during the party.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Drink your drink, enjoy the lamps, and let the old history sleep where it lies.
* [Insight DC 13] Watch his eyes and read what holds him back. -> pry_insight_ok | pry_insight_miss
* Forgive us, we didn't mean to pry. -> apologize
* Let it drop. -> menu

~ pry_insight_ok
Narrator: He isn't hiding the truth from you: he reaches back for the memory, finds an empty cupboard where the years ought to be, and covers the hollow with a practiced laugh.
-> apologize

~ pry_insight_miss
Narrator: All you get is a gentleman's polished smile and the clink of ice against crystal, with nothing readable underneath.
-> menu

~ apologize
set gl_pried_forgiven
set phillip_regard += 1
attitude phillip_druskenvald friendly
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: Think nothing of it, old sport, curiosity is a natural vice of the newly arrived.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Consider the slate wiped clean, so long as we stick to lighter toasts from here on.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: There now, all forgotten, darling, and look how the frost is curling on the windowpane!
-> menu

# The Songstress's own hint (Phillip remembers the gramophone in the sleepers): a second route to the token.
~ ask_singer
adela_druskenvald [sad]: Poor dear soul, she's been sitting by that glass humming the same eight bars since we stepped aboard.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: I've never had the nerve to ask her to stop, or to go on.
adela_druskenvald [sly]: Part of me wonders whether a tune caught in a loop like that just needs a proper audience, or the rest of the record.
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: Didn't we hear a gramophone going in the sleepers, darling? A cabin or two along? I could have sworn.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Second cabin on the left, if my ears serve me: brass horn, scratching away to an empty room.
-> menu

~ ask_painting
set gl_painting_asked
set adela_regard += 1
reveal g3_seascape
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Isn't it the bee's knees? It's the sea that moves when you're not looking, catch it out of the corner of your eye and the whitecaps roll right onto the rocks.
adela_druskenvald [sad]: An old sailor out in the cars is pining for the sight of open water? Oh, Philly, that breaks my heart right in two.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Take it off the hook with my blessing, darling, it isn't ours to give but it should go where it's loved.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Lift it carefully, friends. I never mind a sentimental errand.
approve delphine_ravelle +1: You asked Adela's leave before taking her painting
-> menu

~ leave
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Do come back and tell us everything you find out there in the cars, darling!
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Until the next round, my friends, keep your hats on straight.
-> END

# --- Coming back ---

~ return_router
if flag.gl_pried and not flag.gl_pried_forgiven and not flag.gl_cooler_seen
-> cooler
endif
if flag.gl_songstress_sang and not flag.gl_return_songstress_seen
-> return_songstress
endif
if flag.gl_painting_given and not flag.gl_return_painting_seen
-> return_painting
endif
if flag.haints_destroyed >= 1 and not flag.gl_return_destroyed_seen
-> return_destroyed
endif
-> return

~ return
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Back again, old sports? The ice is still cold and the chairs haven't wandered off.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, swell, I was hoping you hadn't forgotten us so soon!
-> menu

~ return_songstress
set gl_return_songstress_seen
set adela_regard += 1
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Oh, my stars, I am still completely out of breath! When she found the rest of her melody, Philly swept me right out onto the carpet.
adela_druskenvald [sad]: I don't think I've heard anything half so lovely or half so heartbreaking in all my nights.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Well, when a lady sings like that, a man would be a scoundrel not to offer his arm for a turn.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: You did a fine thing for her, friends, and we are both in your debt.
-> menu

~ return_painting
set gl_return_painting_seen
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Look at that bare patch on the ebony, Philly, the wall looks positively naked without its waves!
adela_druskenvald [smile]: I don't mind a bit, darling, so long as your old mariner got his sunset back.
-> menu

~ return_destroyed
set gl_return_destroyed_seen
set phillip_regard -= 1
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: Word travels quick along the floorboards, friends, and it sounds like you've been clearing the cars with a heavy hand.
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: Putting restless souls down by force seems an awfully ill-tempered way of doing things on a passenger line.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Now hush, Philly, we weren't there in the dark with them, and I'm sure our friends only swung when they had to.
-> menu

~ cooler
set gl_cooler_seen
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: Ah. You've returned.
phillip_druskenvald [neutral]: The bar remains open, of course, though I find myself somewhat short on small talk.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Don't mind Philly when he gets his frosty face on, darlings, tell me how you're getting along.
-> menu
